Below we see the unsorted array with the first element highlighted.

===

## Bubble Sort - After First Pass

@use arrayDisplay values="[2, 5, 1, 8, 9]" highlight="9"

After the first pass, the largest element (9) has bubbled to the end.

===

## Bubble Sort - Implementation

@use codeSnippet language="python" title="Bubble Sort Algorithm" code="def bubble_sort(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(0, n-i-1):
            if arr[j] > arr[j+1]:
                arr[j], arr[j+1] = arr[j+1], arr[j]
    return arr"

The classic sorting algorithm with nested loops for comparison.

```python [highlight:line-by-line]
def bubble_sort(arr):
    n = len(arr)
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(0, n-i-1):
            if arr[j] > arr[j+1]:
                arr[j], arr[j+1] = arr[j+1], arr[j]
    return arr
```

===

## Quick Sort - Initial Array

