## Algorithm Steps

@use stepCard number="1" title="Choose Pivot" content="Select the first element as the pivot"

@use stepCard number="2" title="Partition" content="Rearrange elements smaller than pivot to the left, larger to the right"

@use stepCard number="3" title="Recursion" content="Recursively apply the same process to sub-arrays"

===

## Quick Sort - Complete Implementation

@use algorithmCard name="Quick Sort" complexity="O(n log n) average" code="def quick_sort(arr):
    if len(arr) <= 1:
        return arr
    pivot = arr[len(arr) // 2]
    left = [x for x in arr if x < pivot]
    middle = [x for x in arr if x == pivot]
    right = [x for x in arr if x > pivot]
    return quick_sort(left) + middle + quick_sort(right)" description="Divide-and-conquer algorithm using a pivot element to partition the array"

===

## Algorithm Comparison

@use comparisonTable algorithm1="Bubble Sort" time1="O(n²)" space1="O(1)" algorithm2="Quick Sort" time2="O(n log n)" space2="O(log n)"

Side-by-side complexity analysis helps choose the right algorithm.

